1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,570
Audit reports say “Fixed”.

2
00:00:01,570 --> 00:00:02,740
Users trust it.

3
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:06,050
Nobody checks the code that's actually deployed.

4
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:06,780
FixCheck does.

5
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:10,210
It took 22 findings that Sherlock reports mark as fixed,

6
00:00:10,210 --> 00:00:13,630
and read the code at each protocol's own listed address.

7
00:00:13,630 --> 00:00:17,280
12 are confirmed in deployed code; 8 are not.

8
00:00:17,333 --> 00:00:22,853
This is PoolTogether: one row per finding, its status, and how it was decided.

9
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:24,590
This finding was marked fixed.

10
00:00:24,590 --> 00:00:27,640
On the left is the function the auditors reviewed;

11
00:00:27,640 --> 00:00:30,340
on the right, the one deployed on Arbitrum.

12
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:32,620
They're identical, line for line.

13
00:00:32,667 --> 00:00:36,217
Against the fix commit, the fixed line simply isn't there.

14
00:00:36,217 --> 00:00:38,917
So code alone says: not fixed.

15
00:00:38,967 --> 00:00:42,617
When deployed code matches neither version, validators ask a model.

16
00:00:42,617 --> 00:00:45,547
It must quote exact deployed lines, highlighted here,

17
00:00:45,547 --> 00:00:49,017
and code checks they point at the fix.

18
00:00:49,067 --> 00:00:53,667
To check a finding yourself, pick the report, the finding and the deployed address.

19
00:00:53,667 --> 00:00:58,187
Before you pay, the app runs the same checks the contract will.

20
00:00:58,233 --> 00:01:00,533
Then you stake that it isn't fixed.

21
00:01:00,533 --> 00:01:06,013
Every validator fetches the report, both commits and the verified source, and they must agree.

22
00:01:06,067 --> 00:01:07,257
The check is filed.

23
00:01:07,257 --> 00:01:11,087
Anyone can stake that it is fixed until the window closes.

24
00:01:11,133 --> 00:01:12,943
Code decides everything it can.

25
00:01:12,943 --> 00:01:18,213
The model never decides what counts as evidence, the deadlines, or the money.

26
00:01:18,267 --> 00:01:20,307
The real result: PoolTogether's prize pool,

27
00:01:20,307 --> 00:01:26,427
vault and draw manager on OP Mainnet were deployed before the audit and still run the audited code.

28
00:01:26,427 --> 00:01:29,047
The redeployed claimer has its fixes.

29
00:01:29,100 --> 00:01:30,640
Code compares the functions.

30
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:35,650
GenLayer validators only judge the middle cases, and must quote the exact lines.

31
00:01:35,650 --> 00:01:38,750
fixcheck-ledger dot vercel dot app.
